  "content": "Unusual snowfall in Khumbu in first week of October\nRastriya Samachar Samiti (RSS)\nTuesday, October 7, 2025\n0\nComments\nSolukhumbu, October 7\nThe autumn tourist season has begun in the Everest region, usually marked by bustling activity among tourists, traders, and locals along the Namche Bazaar–Gokyo–Dingboche–Phorche route. However, this year, the Khumbu region was blanketed in white following an unusual snowfall in the first week of October.\nSnowfall this early in the season is rare for the region and has affected locals, business owners, and expedition teams. Following heavy rain that began last Sunday morning, snow accumulated in areas above Namche, particularly in Solukhumbu’s Pasanglhamu Rural Municipality.\nLocal resident Pasang Sherpa reported that continuous rain and snow have covered Dingboche, Labuche, Phereche, and Gokyo. Laxman Adhikari, chairperson of Khumbu Pasanglhamu Rural Municipality–4, said the snowfall led to over four feet of snow accumulating on rooftops in upper Khumbu. “The snow that fell above Namche has disrupted daily life,” Adhikari said.\nAccording to the District Police Office, five hotels in the Dingboche area collapsed under the weight of snow.DSP Manojit Kunwar said, “The roofs of five hotels were damaged due to the heavy snow and continuous rainfall. While there have been no human casualties, the economic losses are significant.”\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nElection Commission\nshare market\nGen Z\nlichhibari land scam\nRastriya Samachar Samiti (RSS)\nRSS is a government-run national news portal of Nepal.\nMore From the Author\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nHeavy snowfall affects tourists, locals in Khumbu area\n5 months ago\nKhumbu icefall route readied for ascent to Mt Everest\n6 months a